{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015m2VhnKrCmNzvSJrosjaBx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-285 — the integrator's composed-tree bar never runs (stack.ini schema mismatch)\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-285 · **Status:** queued · **Priority 1** (integration-time gate\n4\tverification is silently OFF) · **Delivers:** SR-006-adjacent (the integrator's\n5\tcombined bar) — harness layer, no new spine SR\n6\t\n7\t## Problem\n8\t\n9\t`agent_dispatch._run_combined_bar` — the composed-tree bar the serialized\n10\tintegrator runs before publishing a train (spec §9, \"combined bar always runs\")\n11\t— reads the test command from `docs/stack.ini` **`[stack] test`**. This repo's\n12\t`stack.ini` has **no `[stack]` section**: it declares the harness under\n13\t**`[product] test = {py} -m pytest -q -n auto`** (with `[tiers] smoke = -m\n14\tsmoke`), the form `check.py` reads and `{py}`/`{src}`/`{tests}`-substitutes.\n15\t\n16\tResult (verified live, run `20260723T0202`): every integration in this repo\n17\tjournals `integration-bar: \"skipped (no declared test command)\"` and treats it as\n18\ta **pass** — so **WI-275, WI-279, and every historical integration landed on\n19\t`llm/integration` without the composed-tree bar ever running.** Integration-time\n20\tgate verification is effectively disabled for the meta-repo (the per-commit\n21\tpre-commit floor still runs on worker commits, but the *combined* bar on the\n22\tmerged tree — the one that catches cross-WI composition breakage — does not).\n23\t\n24\tTwo coupled defects:\n25\t1. **Schema mismatch:** the integrator's contract (`[stack] test`, raw\n26\t   `shlex.split`, no substitution) does not match the kit's own stack.ini schema\n27\t   (`[product] test` with `{py}` placeholders that `check.py` fills). The kit\n28\t   doesn't run its own integrator bar — a dogfood hole.\n29\t2. **Fail-OPEN default:** an absent command returns `(True, \"skipped\")` — a\n30\t   missing bar silently passes. For a walk-away integrator that is the wrong\n31\t   default when a command *should* exist.\n32\t\n33\t## Approach\n34\t\n35\t- **Run the harness the repo actually declares.** Make `_run_combined_bar` invoke\n36\t  the same bar `check.py` does — either read `[product] test` with the `{py}`/\n37\t  `{src}`/`{tests}` substitution (and choose the tier: at minimum smoke, ideally\n38\t  the gate bar `check.py --gate <derived>` on the composed tree), or shell out to\n39\t  `check.py` directly so the integrator and the commit floor share one definition\n40\t  (the WI-260 \"one rule, read once\" precedent).\n41\t- **Tighten the skip:** distinguish \"no harness declared at all\" (a genuinely\n42\t  stackless fixture → legitimately skip) from \"a harness is declared but under a\n43\t  key I didn't read\" (→ do not silently pass). Absent `[product] test` AND absent\n44\t  `[stack] test` = skip; either present = run it.\n45\t- **Dogfood + template decision:** decide whether the fix ships in the kit\n46\t  template (so downstream integrators run their declared bar too) and whether the\n47\t  template's stack schema needs a documented single test-command home; record it.\n48\t- Tests: a stack.ini with `[product] test` must cause the integrator bar to RUN\n49\t  (not skip); the stackless-fixture skip stays; a composed tree that fails the\n50\t  bar parks the train (not integrates).\n51\t\n52\t## Interfaces\n53\t\n54\tNo cross-module seam — intra-module (`agent_dispatch._run_combined_bar` +\n55\t`check.py`/`stack.ini` reading, and tests). Nearest: SR-006 (gate/tier harness),\n56\twhose command home this aligns the integrator with.\n57\t\n58\t## Done-when\n59\t\n60\t- [x] The integrator runs the repo's declared bar on the composed tree (verified:\n61\t      a real integration in this repo journals a RUN result, not \"skipped\" —\n62\t      `test_product_schema_bar_runs_on_real_integration` asserts every\n63\t      `integration-bar` event reads `result: \"pass\"`, never `skipped …`).\n64\t- [x] A composed tree that fails the bar parks the train instead of integrating\n65\t      (`test_combined_bar_product_red_parks` + the existing red-`[stack]` path).\n66\t- [x] The \"declared-but-unread key\" case no longer fail-opens: `[product] test`\n67\t      now RUNS (`test_combined_bar_runs_product_schema_not_skips`), and a\n68\t      declared-but-EMPTY command fails closed rather than skipping\n69\t      (`test_combined_bar_declared_but_empty_fails_closed`).\n70\t- [x] Template/downstream disposition recorded (see Resolution below).\n71\t- [ ] Commit bar green; row `done`, spec archived. _(row-flip + archive are the\n72\t      integrator's close-ritual at done-flip; the worker ran the full suite green:\n73\t      1406 passed, 5 skipped.)_\n74\t\n75\t## Resolution\n76\t\n77\t**What ran vs. where the logic lives.** `_run_combined_bar` now resolves the\n78\tdeclared test command through a new `agent_common._declared_test_command(ini)`:\n79\tthe kit schema `[product] test` (with the same `{py}/{src}/{tests}` substitution\n80\t`check.py` applies for its `tests+coverage` step), with the legacy raw `[stack]\n81\ttest` kept as a fallback. The skip is honest — **only** a profile declaring\n82\tNEITHER key skips; a key present under a name the integrator didn't read (or an\n83\tempty command) no longer silently passes (empty → fail closed, never\n84\t`subprocess([])`).\n85\t\n86\t**Why `agent_common`, not `import check`.** The first cut imported `check`\n87\tdirectly (\"one rule, read once\"), but `check.py` is CMP-001 and `agent_dispatch`\n88\tis CMP-004, so that in-process import is an undeclared CMP-004→CMP-001 edge that\n89\t`check_trajectory --strict` (the G3 gate) flags. The resolver is used *only* by\n90\tthe integrator (never by `check.steps()`), so housing it in `check.py` would not\n91\thave shared one definition anyway — it would just have added a seam. Instead it\n92\tlives in `agent_common` (the CMP-004 shared-coordinator-primitives module the\n93\tintegrator already imports), mirroring `check.py`'s stack schema the same way\n94\t`OWNER_ONLY_PATHS` mirrors `check_docs.SCRATCHPAD` rather than importing across\n95\tthat boundary; the tokenizer is `agent_session.split_cmd` (no new duplicate), and\n96\tthe tests pin the resolver against drift.\n97\t\n98\t**Template / downstream.** No new schema is needed: `[product] test` is already\n99\tthe single documented test-command home (`stack.ini.template`), and\n100\t`agent_dispatch.py` / `agent_common.py` are kit scripts that ship downstream\n101\tverbatim — so downstream integrators get this fix on re-sync with no migration.\n102\t`[stack] test` remains honored purely as a legacy fallback.\n103\t\n104\t**Known residue (not this WI).** The SSOT ideal — `check.steps()` and the\n105\tintegrator both deriving the base test command from one function — stays deferred\n106\t(`steps()` appends coverage/tier args and can't cleanly reuse the plain\n107\tresolver); worth a follow-up if the integrator↔harness coupling is later blessed\n108\tinto a declared IF-### seam.\n109\t\n110\t## Notes\n111\t\n112\t- Filed 2026-07-23 from the run-babysit (WI-279's skipped bar). `Priority 1`:\n113\t  until this lands, integrations are not gate-verified — the reconcile that\n114\t  surfaced it had to run the full suite by hand to close the gap for WI-279.\n115\t- Interacts with WI-286 (worktree Python): the integrator bar must run under a\n116\t  floor-satisfying interpreter, or it re-introduces the ambient-3.8 risk.\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4520695-cdaf-47f7-b579-0f8123018df3","uuid":"b210eff0-5e80-4dfb-9929-9990978435f6","timestamp":"2026-07-24T07:32:38.948Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\p0-g3-WI-285-76a8\\docs\\specs\\WI-285.md","content":"# WI-285 — the integrator's composed-tree bar never runs (stack.ini schema mismatch)\n\n**WI:** WI-285 · **Status:** queued · **Priority 1** (integration-time gate\nverification is silently OFF) · **Delivers:** SR-006-adjacent (the integrator's\ncombined bar) — harness layer, no new spine SR\n\n## Problem\n\n`agent_dispatch._run_combined_bar` — the composed-tree bar the serialized\nintegrator runs before publishing a train (spec §9, \"combined bar always runs\")\n— reads the test command from `docs/stack.ini` **`[stack] test`**. This repo's\n`stack.ini` has **no `[stack]` section**: it declares the harness under\n**`[product] test = {py} -m pytest -q -n auto`** (with `[tiers] smoke = -m\nsmoke`), the form `check.py` reads and `{py}`/`{src}`/`{tests}`-substitutes.\n\nResult (verified live, run `20260723T0202`): every integration in this repo\njournals `integration-bar: \"skipped (no declared test command)\"` and treats it as\na **pass** — so **WI-275, WI-279, and every historical integration landed on\n`llm/integration` without the composed-tree bar ever running.** Integration-time\ngate verification is effectively disabled for the meta-repo (the per-commit\npre-commit floor still runs on worker commits, but the *combined* bar on the\nmerged tree — the one that catches cross-WI composition breakage — does not).\n\nTwo coupled defects:\n1. **Schema mismatch:** the integrator's contract (`[stack] test`, raw\n   `shlex.split`, no substitution) does not match the kit's own stack.ini schema\n   (`[product] test` with `{py}` placeholders that `check.py` fills). The kit\n   doesn't run its own integrator bar — a dogfood hole.\n2. **Fail-OPEN default:** an absent command returns `(True, \"skipped\")` — a\n   missing bar silently passes. For a walk-away integrator that is the wrong\n   default when a command *should* exist.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Run the harness the repo actually declares.** Make `_run_combined_bar` invoke\n  the same bar `check.py` does — either read `[product] test` with the `{py}`/\n  `{src}`/`{tests}` substitution (and choose the tier: at minimum smoke, ideally\n  the gate bar `check.py --gate <derived>` on the composed tree), or shell out to\n  `check.py` directly so the integrator and the commit floor share one definition\n  (the WI-260 \"one rule, read once\" precedent).\n- **Tighten the skip:** distinguish \"no harness declared at all\" (a genuinely\n  stackless fixture → legitimately skip) from \"a harness is declared but under a\n  key I didn't read\" (→ do not silently pass). Absent `[product] test` AND absent\n  `[stack] test` = skip; either present = run it.\n- **Dogfood + template decision:** decide whether the fix ships in the kit\n  template (so downstream integrators run their declared bar too) and whether the\n  template's stack schema needs a documented single test-command home; record it.\n- Tests: a stack.ini with `[product] test` must cause the integrator bar to RUN\n  (not skip); the stackless-fixture skip stays; a composed tree that fails the\n  bar parks the train (not integrates).\n\n## Interfaces\n\nNo cross-module seam — intra-module (`agent_dispatch._run_combined_bar` +\n`check.py`/`stack.ini` reading, and tests). Nearest: SR-006 (gate/tier harness),\nwhose command home this aligns the integrator with.\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [x] The integrator runs the repo's declared bar on the composed tree (verified:\n      a real integration in this repo journals a RUN result, not \"skipped\" —\n      `test_product_schema_bar_runs_on_real_integration` asserts every\n      `integration-bar` event reads `result: \"pass\"`, never `skipped …`).\n- [x] A composed tree that fails the bar parks the train instead of integrating\n      (`test_combined_bar_product_red_parks` + the existing red-`[stack]` path).\n- [x] The \"declared-but-unread key\" case no longer fail-opens: `[product] test`\n      now RUNS (`test_combined_bar_runs_product_schema_not_skips`), and a\n      declared-but-EMPTY command fails closed rather than skipping\n      (`test_combined_bar_declared_but_empty_fails_closed`).\n- [x] Template/downstream disposition recorded (see Resolution below).\n- [ ] Commit bar green; row `done`, spec archived. _(row-flip + archive are the\n      integrator's close-ritual at done-flip; the worker ran the full suite green:\n      1406 passed, 5 skipped.)_\n\n## Resolution\n\n**What ran vs. where the logic lives.** `_run_combined_bar` now resolves the\ndeclared test command through a new `agent_common._declared_test_command(ini)`:\nthe kit schema `[product] test` (with the same `{py}/{src}/{tests}` substitution\n`check.py` applies for its `tests+coverage` step), with the legacy raw `[stack]\ntest` kept as a fallback. The skip is honest — **only** a profile declaring\nNEITHER key skips; a key present under a name the integrator didn't read (or an\nempty command) no longer silently passes (empty → fail closed, never\n`subprocess([])`).\n\n**Why `agent_common`, not `import check`.** The first cut imported `check`\ndirectly (\"one rule, read once\"), but `check.py` is CMP-001 and `agent_dispatch`\nis CMP-004, so that in-process import is an undeclared CMP-004→CMP-001 edge that\n`check_trajectory --strict` (the G3 gate) flags. The resolver is used *only* by\nthe integrator (never by `check.steps()`), so housing it in `check.py` would not\nhave shared one definition anyway — it would just have added a seam. Instead it\nlives in `agent_common` (the CMP-004 shared-coordinator-primitives module the\nintegrator already imports), mirroring `check.py`'s stack schema the same way\n`OWNER_ONLY_PATHS` mirrors `check_docs.SCRATCHPAD` rather than importing across\nthat boundary; the tokenizer is `agent_session.split_cmd` (no new duplicate), and\nthe tests pin the resolver against drift.\n\n**Template / downstream.** No new schema is needed: `[product] test` is already\nthe single documented test-command home (`stack.ini.template`), and\n`agent_dispatch.py` / `agent_common.py` are kit scripts that ship downstream\nverbatim — so downstream integrators get this fix on re-sync with no migration.\n`[stack] test` remains honored purely as a legacy fallback.\n\n**Known residue (not this WI).** The SSOT ideal — `check.steps()` and the\nintegrator both deriving the base test command from one function — stays deferred\n(`steps()` appends coverage/tier args and can't cleanly reuse the plain\nresolver); worth a follow-up if the integrator↔harness coupling is later blessed\ninto a declared IF-### seam.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Filed 2026-07-23 from the run-babysit (WI-279's skipped bar). `Priority 1`:\n  until this lands, integrations are not gate-verified — the reconcile that\n  surfaced it had to run the full suite by hand to close the gap for WI-279.\n- Interacts with WI-286 (worktree Python): the integrator bar must run under a\n  floor-satisfying interpreter, or it re-introduces the ambient-3.8 risk.\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}}}
